<title>YUGOSLAVIA: Montenegro may buy aircraft to boost tourism.</title>
<headline>Montenegro may buy aircraft to boost tourism.</headline>
<dateline>MILOCER, Montenegro 1996-09-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Montenegro is considering buying three aircraft in a bid to boost its tourism industry, a senior government official said on Monday.</p>
<p>&quot;Montenegro is a typical flight destination. Our tourist capacities can be used in the best possible way only if we fly the tourists in,&quot; Janko Jeknic, foreign minister of Montenegro, now part of rump Yugoslavia along with Serbia, told Reuters.</p>
<p>He said that the Boeing 737, and also Fokker aircraft, were being considered, but gave no further details.</p>
